.TH SYS_PROC_COUNT 2 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_count \- get total number of active processes
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/syscall.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_count(void);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sys_proc_count()
system call returns the total number of active processes in the system.
This includes all processes in RUNNING, READY, SLEEPING, and STOPPED states.
ZOMBIE state processes are excluded from the count.
.PP
This call is useful for monitoring system load and for determining how many
process slots are in use.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, returns the number of active processes (always >= 1, since at
least the calling process exists).
.PP
This function does not fail under normal circumstances.
.SH ERRORS
This system call does not return any errors.
.SH NOTES
The returned count is a snapshot at the time of the call.
The actual number of processes may change immediately after
.B sys_proc_count()
returns.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_proc_info (2),
.BR sys_proc_list (2),
.BR sys_cpu_count (2),
.BR intro (2)
